/* book Worked example 2: Q: 2.0 kg of ground spice holding 5 mass% essential oil is extracted with CO2 at 40 °C and 200 bar. The fluid leaving the bed holds 1.5 mass% oil, taken as its saturation loading at these conditions. Find the CO2 needed to remove all the oil and the time at 5 kg/h of CO2.
   1. Oil = 2.0 × 0.05 = 0.100 kg; inert solid 1.90 kg.
   2. Leaving fluid: 0.015 kg oil per kg of oil-plus-CO2, so 0.100 kg oil needs 0.100/0.015 = 6.67 kg of solution.
   3. CO2 = 6.67 − 0.100 = 6.57 kg. This is a minimum: it assumes the fluid leaves saturated all the time, which holds only while easily reached oil remains.
   4. Time = 6.57/5 = 1.31 h = 78.8 min.
   Answer: At least 6.57 kg of CO2, about 1.31 h at 5 kg/h; in practice the end of the run is diffusion-limited and takes longer. */
