/* book exam traps: Check how the stroke is defined: pulse intensity A·f uses the peak-to-peak stroke; with an amplitude a measured from the mean, the stroke is 2a. | A centrifuge speeds settling; it does not change the tie lines or the number of ideal stages. | Supercritical CO2 is not a gas without solvent power: at 200 bar it is about as dense as a liquid, and its solvent power is adjusted with pressure. | In the CO2 balance use the oil fraction of the leaving fluid (0.015), not that of the feed solid (0.05), and remember 1.5 mass% means per kg of solution, not per kg of CO2. | Saying CO2 removes caffeine because caffeine is non-polar is wrong; caffeine is moderately polar and the process relies on dense CO2 and moisture. */
