/* book exam traps: The overflow from stage 1 (400 kg/h) is not the overflow in the washing stages (600 kg/h): the dry feed's solute dissolves only in stage 1. Using E = 400/450 for the whole battery gives 70.4 % instead of 78.5 %. | Stage 1 is not a washing stage; the Kremser relation covers the N − 1 stages from 2 to N. | In the Shanks system the solid does not move; the inlet and outlet of the liquor are switched round the battery. | Strong liquor leaves from the tank (or stage) holding the freshest solid, not from the one receiving fresh solvent. | Solids and liquor flowing the same way (co-current) give little more than one ideal stage however many tanks are used, because the two streams leave together at the same composition. */
